(e) Average stopping time vs. heuristic
    measured mean tau over [1, N]        = 131.4344
    mean of log2(n) over [1, N]          = 18.4889
    measured mean tau / mean log2(n)     = 7.1088
    naive 1/(1 - log2 3)                 = -1.7095  (negative -> not a valid average)
    Naive 2^K vs 3^K argument: each odd step multiplies by ~3 and
    each even step divides by 2; on average the map shrinks, so the
    average stopping time is expected to grow only logarithmically
    in n. We report the MEASURED ratio above rather than assert it.

